        "original_id": "f6472c05-269e-5783-958e-8582e5e4a41b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sathish Kalathil, Jacques Feyder, Alexandre Arnoux, Charles Spaak, Maurice Constantin-Weyer\n- Films: Jalachhayam, Veena Vaadanam, La Loi du nord\n- Topics: Malayalam cinema, experimental films, documentary films, French adventure drama films\n\nFacts:\n- Jacques Feyder was a Belgian actor, screenwriter, and film director who was born on 21 July 1885 and died on 24 May 1948.\n- Jacques Feyder worked principally in France and also worked in the USA, Britain, and Germany.\n- La Loi du nord is a 1939 French adventure drama film directed by Jacques Feyder.\n- La Loi du nord was also called La Piste du Nord and was co-written by Jacques Feyder, Alexandre Arnoux, and Charles Spaak.\n- La Loi du nord was based on the novel \"Telle qu'elle était de son vivant\" by Maurice Constantin-Weyer.\n- Jalachhayam is Sathish Kalathil's 2010 debut movie.\n- Sathish Kalathil's experimental works are well known and discussed in the Malayalam cinema industry.\n- Jalachhayam was discussed for its experimental approach.\n- Veena Vaadanam, also called Recital of Music, is an Indian documentary film in the Malayalam language directed by Sathish Kalathil.",
